      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e17826fa-50b5-51fe-abb3-c5d89f2defd7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marcia Wallace, David Silverman, Rich Moore, Phil Johnston, Jennifer Lee, Jim Reardon, Dan Castellaneta, Julie Kavner, Nancy Cartwright, Yeardley Smith, Hank Azaria, Harry Shearer, Tress MacNeille, Pamela Hayden, Maggie Roswell, Russi Taylor, Tom Hanks, Albert Brooks\n- Characters: Edna Krabappel, Bart Simpson, Ned Flanders\n- Works: The Bob Newhart Show, The Simpsons, The Simpsons Movie, Wreck-It Ralph, Futurama\n- Places: Springfield Elementary School\n- Roles: Carol Kester, elementary school teacher, 4th grade class teacher\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1970s, Marcia Wallace played receptionist Carol Kester on the sitcom \"The Bob Newhart Show\".\n- In 1992, Marcia Wallace won an Emmy for voicing Edna Krabappel on the animated series \"The Simpsons\".\n- Marcia Wallace is best known for playing Carol Kester on \"The Bob Newhart Show\" and for voicing Edna Krabappel on \"The Simpsons\".\n- Edna Krabappel is the teacher of Bart Simpson's 4th grade class at Springfield Elementary School.\n- In later seasons of \"The Simpsons\", Edna Krabappel becomes Ned Flanders's wife.\n- \"The Simpsons Movie\" was directed by David Silverman.\n- \"The Simpsons Movie\" features the regular television cast including Dan Castellaneta, Julie Kavner, Nancy Cartwright, Yeardley Smith, Hank Azaria, Harry Shearer, Tress MacNeille, Pamela Hayden, Marcia Wallace, Maggie Roswell, and Russi Taylor, along with Tom Hanks, Green Day, and Albert Brooks.\n- \"Wreck-It Ralph\" was directed by Rich Moore.\n- Rich Moore had directed episodes of \"The Simpsons\" and \"Futurama\" before directing \"Wreck-It Ralph\".\n- The screenplay for \"Wreck-It Ralph\" was written by Phil Johnston and Jennifer Lee from a story by Rich Moore, Phil Johnston, and Jim Reardon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ed52daa4-761d-58a4-a301-1bac044d6ed4",
        "text": "Page: Marcia Wallace. Sentence: She is perhaps best known for her roles as receptionist Carol Kester on the 1970s sitcom \"The Bob Newhart Show\", and as the voice of elementary school teacher Edna Krabappel on the animated series \"The Simpsons\", for which she won an Emmy in 1992.\nPage: Edna Krabappel. Sentence: She is the teacher of Bart Simpson's 4th grade class at Springfield Elementary School, and Ned Flanders's wife in later seasons.\nPage: The Simpsons Movie. Sentence: The film was directed by David Silverman, and stars the regular television cast of Dan Castellaneta, Julie Kavner, Nancy Cartwright, Yeardley Smith, Hank Azaria, Harry Shearer, Tress MacNeille, Pamela Hayden, Marcia Wallace, Maggie Roswell and Russi Taylor, along with Tom Hanks, Green Day and Albert Brooks.\nPage: Wreck-It Ralph. Sentence: The film was directed by Rich Moore, who has directed episodes of \"The Simpsons\" and \"Futurama\", and the screenplay was written by Phil Johnston and Jennifer Lee from a story by Moore, Johnston, and Jim Reardon.",
